
TITLE:: Client
summary:: represents a remote sclang application
categories:: Networking
related:: Classes/LocalClient, Guides/Glossary

DESCRIPTION::
Client and LocalClient together represent a sender / receiver pair for sclang side OSC messages.
Using SynthDef-like global function definitions, ClientFunc, an sclang application
can evaluate code on a remote sclang app.

For examples, see link::Classes/LocalClient::.


CLASSMETHODS::

private:: initClass

METHOD:: named
dictionary of all named instances of Client

METHOD:: new
returns a new instance and stores it in global dictionary all.
the port is set to defaultPort, which is hardcoded presently.
if no address is passed in, localhost is used.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: send
evaluates a client function that is stored at that key

METHOD:: password
get and set password for interpreter access

METHOD:: cmdName
		set the cmdName under which the client sends (default: '/client')
		this cmdName must be the same as the LocalClient receiver cmdName.

METHOD:: interpret
		if the remote client has the same password, it interprets  the string

METHOD:: verbose
get set flag whether to post info

METHOD:: defaultAddr, defaultPort
the default (local) address and port to use

METHOD:: name
the client's name (a Symbol)

METHOD:: addr
argument:: address
the client's NetAddress

private:: prepareSendBundle, sendBundle, recv, interpret
private:: minit, remove, add, sendTo
